{"name":"Bonza Green","hex":"#5e6b44","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bonza","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of bonzer."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of bonzer.","A reddish apple originating in Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bonza"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bonza","blocks":[{"text":"Bonza Aviation Pty Ltd, operating as Bonza, was a short-lived Australian low-cost airline, headquartered on the Sunshine Coast. Founded in October 2021, Bonza commenced operations on 31 January 2023. The airline entered voluntary administration on 30 April 2024 suspending all services, after several aircraft were repossessed. It was placed in liquidation on 2 July 2024 after laying off its workforce and failing to find a buyer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d5/Bonza_%28airline%29_logo.svg/330px-Bonza_%28airline%29_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonza","wikidata":"Q109312519"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Bonza_Airlines_%28VH-UKH%29_Boeing_737_MAX_8_parked_at_Sunshine_Coast_Airport.jpg/500px-Bonza_Airlines_%28VH-UKH%29_Boeing_737_MAX_8_parked_at_Sunshine_Coast_Airport.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Bonza_Airlines_%28VH-UKH%29_Boeing_737_MAX_8_parked_at_Sunshine_Coast_Airport.jpg/1280px-Bonza_Airlines_%28VH-UKH%29_Boeing_737_MAX_8_parked_at_Sunshine_Coast_Airport.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Bonza_Airlines_%28VH-UKH%29_Boeing_737_MAX_8_parked_at_Sunshine_Coast_Airport.jpg/500px-Bonza_Airlines_%28VH-UKH%29_Boeing_737_MAX_8_parked_at_Sunshine_Coast_Airport.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bonza Boeing 737 MAX 8 parked at Sunshine Coast Airport","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABonza_Airlines_(VH-UKH)_Boeing_737_MAX_8_parked_at_Sunshine_Coast_Airport.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Bonza_plane_Avalon_2.jpg/500px-Bonza_plane_Avalon_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai